# `yo test` synthesizes each batch's `main` with `io :: __yo_builtin_io;` so a
# test body can use `io` (or an implicit `using(io : Io)` can find it). A batch
# whose tests never name `io` printed `warning: unused variable \`io\`` for the
# generated binding; the runner now also emits `_yo_batch_io :: io;`
# (issues/fixed/yo-test-warns-about-its-own-io-binding.md). The golden keeps the
# verdicts and any unused-variable warning, so the warning's return is a diff.
stdout_keep=^(  ✓|  ✗|[0-9]+ passed|[0-9]+ failed|warning: unused variable)
timeout=300
